 =?UTF-8?q?MIDI=20source=20dir=20env=20var=20(W22-WB-E=20A/B)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0107, Phase 10 W22-WB-E A/B comparison). Adds
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE env var to switch between two
MIDI directories at SoundManager::init: 'wiimidi' (default) -> data/
midi/ (WiiWare arrangements per scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py); 'orgmid'
-> data/midi-orgmid/ (literal ORGMID transcription per scripts/
build-cs-midi-orgmid.py; transposed +12 to fix octave-down quirk).

Operator-controllable for next-iter A/B real-HW listening between
the WiiWare arrangement aesthetic vs literal-ORGMID transcription
on g2k Vibra16S OPL3 + DreamBlaster S2. Decide canonical set based
on listening, not theory.

Scope (per team-lead 2026-05-07 dispatch):
- 1 new private member: SoundManager::_midi_source_dir (default "midi")
- env-var resolution at SoundManager::init (~30 LOC including narration)
- _start_mid_track() uses _midi_source_dir + "/" + name + ".mid"
- LOG_WARN message updated to include the resolved dir name
- docs/BOOT.md entry under user-facing options

Recognized values:
  unset / "wiimidi" / empty -> "midi"        (data/midi/<n>.mid; default)
  "orgmid"                  -> "midi-orgmid" (data/midi-orgmid/<n>.mid)
  any other value           -> "midi" (fallback + LOG_INFO unrecognized)

Resolved ONCE at SoundManager::init (not per-track-load); cached in
_midi_source_dir. Banner log fires at startup so flush-instr +
debugging can see which set is in use without diffing audio output.

Has no effect when AUDIO_BACKEND=organya (Organya path doesn't use
.mid files). Affects only MidiScheduler-routed backends (midi-stub
/ wb / opl3).

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, 5 gates):
  Gate 1 -- env unset (organya default + wiimidi banner): both
    log lines present; "MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'wiimidi'
    (default;...)" appears even though Organya path is selected
    (init logs the resolved dir regardless of backend so operator
    can see what would be used if a MIDI backend were active).
    37 flips, no crashes.
  Gate 2 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=wb + MIDI_SOURCE unset: "MidiScheduler:
    MIDI source = 'wiimidi'" + MidiBackendWaveBlaster armed; music
    dispatch routes through data/midi/<name>.mid. 38 flips.
  Gate 3 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=wb + AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE=orgmid: banner
    shows "MIDI source = 'orgmid' (resolves to data/midi-orgmid/...)";
    MidiBackendWaveBlaster armed; path resolution would use data/
    midi-orgmid/. 40 flips. (Real-HW iter populates the dir via
    scripts/build-cs-midi-orgmid.py before launching.)
  Gate 4 -- explicit MIDI_SOURCE=wiimidi: same as Gate 1 banner.
    36 flips.
  Gate 5 -- invalid value 'garbage': "MidiScheduler: unrecognized
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE value 'garbage'; falling
    back to 'wiimidi' (data/midi/)." 37 flips.

  All 5 gates PASS.

strings-grep verifies banner text + value labels + fallback message
all present in binary.

Out of scope (per team-lead's "scope is exactly the path-switch +
log line + docs entry"):
  - data/midi-orgmid/ population -- handled by separate script
    scripts/build-cs-midi-orgmid.py (just landed per team-lead)
  - MidiScheduler-internal changes (path-resolution stays in
    SoundManager::_start_mid_track per slot 0101 architecture)
  - Per-track override (orgmid for some tracks, wiimidi for others)
    -- not needed; A/B comparison is whole-set basis
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/sound/SoundManager.h   |  9 +++++++
 2 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index 8c9a147..5330fb9 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -338,6 +338,46 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
   // 2/3/4 (patches 0101+) plug the actual backend implementations.
   selectBackendFromEnv();
 
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0107, Phase 10 W22-WB-E A/B): resolve MIDI source
+  // directory once per process. Default = "midi" (data/midi/, the
+  // wiimidi-arrangement set from scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py per
+  // docs/ASSETS.md Step 4.5). Operator-controllable via
+  // SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE for W22-WB-E A/B comparison
+  // between WiiWare arrangements and literal-ORGMID transcriptions.
+  // Resolved here once at init so _start_mid_track() does not re-
+  // read the env var on every song change (cleaner than per-call
+  // SDL_GetHint + cheaper than SDL_GetHint anyway). The cached
+  // dir name is logged at startup so flush-instr / debugging can
+  // see which set was in use without diffing audio output.
+  {
+    const char *src = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE");
+    if (src == nullptr || src[0] == '\0' || std::strcmp(src, "wiimidi") == 0)
+    {
+      _midi_source_dir = "midi";
+      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'wiimidi' "
+               "(default; resolves to data/midi/<name>.mid; the WiiWare "
+               "arrangement set fetched by scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py per "
+               "docs/ASSETS.md Step 4.5).");
+    }
+    else if (std::strcmp(src, "orgmid") == 0)
+    {
+      _midi_source_dir = "midi-orgmid";
+      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'orgmid' "
+               "(resolves to data/midi-orgmid/<name>.mid; literal ORGMID "
+               "transcription set generated by scripts/build-cs-midi-"
+               "orgmid.py -- alternative to the WiiWare arrangements for "
+               "W22-WB-E A/B comparison; transposed +12 to match Cave "
+               "Story canonical pitch).");
+    }
+    else
+    {
+      _midi_source_dir = "midi";
+      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: unrecognized SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_"
+               "SOURCE value '{}'; falling back to 'wiimidi' (data/midi/). "
+               "Recognized values: wiimidi (default) | orgmid.", src);
+    }
+  }
+
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0104, Phase 10 Stage 5 auto-detect chain):
   // refactored backend-install dispatch. Per-backend installation
   // logic lives in file-scope helpers (_try_install_*) so the auto-
@@ -802,8 +842,11 @@ void SoundManager::_start_mid_track(int songno, bool resume)
     return;
   }
 
+  // patch 0107: use _midi_source_dir resolved at init from SDL_HINT_-
+  // DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE. Default = "midi" (data/midi/);
+  // "orgmid" -> "midi-orgmid" (data/midi-orgmid/).
   const std::string path = ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(
-      "midi/" + _music_names[songno] + ".mid", false);
+      _midi_source_dir + "/" + _music_names[songno] + ".mid", false);
   if (MidiScheduler::getInstance()->load(path))
   {
     MidiScheduler::getInstance()->start();
@@ -812,8 +855,8 @@ void SoundManager::_start_mid_track(int songno, bool resume)
   {
     LOG_WARN("SoundManager::_start_mid_track: could not load '{}' "
              "(songno={}); music slot stays silent. Verify "
-             "scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py was run + data/midi/ contains "
-             "the file.", path, songno);
+             "scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py was run + data/{}/ contains "
+             "the file.", path, songno, _midi_source_dir);
   }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.h b/src/sound/SoundManager.h
index f785ea7..d2cd0f0 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.h
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.h
@@ -228,6 +228,15 @@ private:
   std::vector<std::string> _music_dir_names;
   std::vector<std::string> _music_playlists;
 
+  // patch 0107 (Phase 10 W22-WB-E A/B): per-process MIDI source-dir
+  // selection via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE. Resolved once
+  // at SoundManager::init() and stored here; _start_mid_track() uses
+  // this dir name (no trailing slash) when constructing the .mid
+  // file path. Default empty string sentinel = "midi" (the existing
+  // wiimidi-arrangement set fetched by scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py per
+  // docs/ASSETS.md Step 4.5). Documented in docs/BOOT.md.
+  std::string _midi_source_dir = "midi";
+
   const char _bossmusic[14] = {4, 7, 10, 11, 15, 16, 17, 18, 21, 22, 31, 33, 35, 0};
 };
 
